I've always been a huge fan of the Borderlands franchise. Back when this game was announced I already was excited for it, yet it was even better than expected.
An interactive movie of approx 10 hours for 23 bucks. It had awesomely well designed characters, an insane amount of hilarious scenes packed with a♥♥♥♥♥♥ton of references and jokes, a gripping story (warning: plottwists everywhere) AND still managed to give you so many feels ;__;
To be honest I found this game so good that I saved up the last season for multiple weeks just because I didn't want it to end. Only bad thing about this game that I can say is that in season 5 the amount of tiny bugs (for instance character models being loaded late and subtitles being off) increased. But in the end everything about this game fit so well together that that's completely irrelevant - even the graphics and animations got a lot better in comparison to older Telltale Games.

I have thought that the idea of racing with planes, boats and cars was original for Sumo. It appears it isn't. There was some old game which had the same feature, though the forms weren't changing during race.
Anyway, The game has a lot of things to offer, such as:
- Unique racing mechanics;
- Exciting All-star moves;
- Great characters (of course there will be always most and least favourite character);
- Challenging career and bots;
- Grand prix races (4 races in a row);
- Time attack is like "become a pro" training (note: going for expert times is REALLY hard!);
- Vehicle customisation, and by that I mean changing the way your vehicle is handling;
- Multiplayer is still alive. I also believe that people keep organising tournaments;
- A somewhat reliable way of judging people's skill. You can check other's licence, which will give you overall stats, such as total time played, beaten staff ghosts (time attacks), career progression etc.
There is probably more of that, but at the time of writing it I can't think of anything else.
Of course the game isn't perfect. There are some flaws, such as:
- You may get stuck at some tougher missions in career;
- At least two time trials can get really frustrating (Sanctuary Falls and Chilly Castle);
- Getting outplayed by pros (hint: go for mastering career and some time trials);
Uhh... come to think about it, these flaws are not so bad. You just need to approach them properly and they shouldn't be a problem. Skill won't come so easily after all.
It is way better than it was after release. You want to know why? Check my screenshots for this game to find out. This game had a lot of crashes and glitches back then... but it was then. Everything is great now.
So summing up, it's a great game and if you enjoy gokart games, you won't be disappointed with this game.
Also on the side note, if you plan on buying some DLCs, buy only Metal Sonic + Outrun Bay DLC. The other two are just weird and don't fit into the game.

A very fun kart racing game available on PC:
*Solid mechanics;
*Good controls (although using a controller is a must);
*Decent presentation;
*The soundtrack is fitting;
*Runs smoothly.
My only major complaint is that it is a bit too easy.
I still think you should be able to unlock content even when playing online with a friend, but I digress.
It's a great game, I definitely recommend it if you're looking for an arcade racing game or a serviceable substitute for Mario Kart.

